<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Eshrefids</h1><p class="st-meta">1285 CE – 1326 CE · capital Beyşehir</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived beylik on Lake Beysehir whose wooden-columned Eshrefoglu Mosque is a World Heritage Site.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Eshrefids descended from Eshref, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> commander serving the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sultanate-of-rum">Sultanate of Rum</a>. In the 1280s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sayf-al-din-suleyman-bey">Sayf al-Din Suleyman Bey</a> made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beysehir">Beysehir</a> on the lake of the same name the centre of a principality as Seljuk power waned.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a> held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beysehir">Beysehir</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seydisehir">Seydisehir</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksehir">Aksehir</a> at times. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sayf-al-din-suleyman-bey">Suleyman Bey</a> built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esrefoglu-mosque">Eshrefoglu Mosque</a> in 1296-1299, whose interior has a forest of carved cedar columns and painted wooden ceilings, among the finest surviving wooden mosques; it was listed with other Anatolian wooden mosques as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">World Heritage Site</a> in 2023. The beylik had little political weight among its neighbours.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1326 the Ilkhanid governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timurtash-chupanid">Timurtash</a>, executed its last ruler, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suleyman-ii-of-eshref">Suleyman II</a>, and the lands passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hamidids">Hamidids</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/eshrefids.jpg" alt="Eshrefids" width="320" height="161"><figcaption>Image: Kılıç46 · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:E%C5%9Frefo%C4%9Fullar%C4%B1_Beyli%C4%9Fi%27nin_konumu.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1285 CE – 1326 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Beyşehir</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sayf al-Din Suleyman Bey, Mubariz al-Din Mehmed Bey, Suleyman II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Turkish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Eşrefoğulları</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1306&amp;focus=eshrefids" aria-label="Eshrefids on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5472 822 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Eshrefids lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5792 1078L6134 1224"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6134 1224h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5792 1078h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5792 1078h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Beyşehir. <a href="/atlas?year=1306&amp;focus=eshrefids">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

